XR ambience layer with hysteresis: a frame with nothing of it to draw keeps the buffer's size

WakerQuest 1.1.8. The screen mode's ambience (patch 0034) added its two eyes to the buffer only in the
frames that had something to draw (an actor near the screen); with none, the buffer lost two eyes, and
the XR layer recreated its swapchain and re-imported the buffers at every change (137 recreations in a
session where there was nothing to draw at all).

- encode_ambient: once the layer is on, a frame with nothing to draw does not drop it: the screen's
  picture is kept aside as ever and the ambience's two eyes are cleared to transparent (clear_ambient_eyes,
  two empty passes), so the buffer, its size and the eyes' places stay. Off, once, after 3 s without a
  draw; back on at the first frame with one. Both changes are logged.

diff --git a/lib/gfx/encoding.cpp b/lib/gfx/encoding.cpp
--- a/lib/gfx/encoding.cpp
+++ b/lib/gfx/encoding.cpp
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <array>
